# Phase 4a spike, item 5 (spec section 12), second half: the asset
# manifest gen/assets.rb would write, a 200-arm `case` from logical to
# digested path, compiled. A record, not a test.
#
# The module was generated by a ten-line script (not kept): logical paths
# stylesheets/asset_000.css, javascripts/asset_001.js, images/
# asset_002.png, fonts/asset_003.woff2 ... fonts/asset_199.woff2, each
# digest the first 8 hex characters of SHA-256 of its logical path (a
# stand-in for the file's).
#
# Run (Spinel 2026.11.04.7026, from spikes/phase4/):
#   time spinel $(spin flags) asset_case.rb -o /tmp/asset_case && ls -l /tmp/asset_case && /tmp/asset_case
# Output (1.29 s to compile, a 429,272-byte binary; one cloud vCPU):
#   arms: 200, hits: 200, miss: ""
#   first: /assets/stylesheets/asset_000-5d43ab26.css
#   last: /assets/fonts/asset_199-1f46d4d9.woff2
#   1000000 lookups: 293 ns each (39500000 bytes)
# The same program with a 1-arm case (ARMS = 1): 1.20 s, 384,880 bytes,
# 13 ns a lookup; so the 200 arms add about 0.1 s and 44 KB, and a lookup
# walks the arms in order (CRuby 3.3.6, which hashes a `case` of String
# literals, takes 183 ns a lookup for the 200-arm program).
